Implementing large file slice uploading and breakpoint continuation (resumable uploads) requires coordination between the frontend and the backend. 

Here is a complete, executable demonstration. It includes a **Vue 3 (Composition API)** frontend and a simple **Node.js (Express)** backend to handle the file chunks and merging.

### 1. Frontend: Vue 3 Implementation

First, install the required dependencies in your Vue project:
```bash
npm install axios spark-md5
```

Create a component named `LargeFileUpload.vue`:

```vue
<template>
  <div class="upload-container">
    <h2>Large File Slice Upload & Breakpoint Continuation</h2>

    <input type="file" @change="handleFileChange" :disabled="status === 'uploading'" />

    <div class="controls" v-if="file">
      <button @click="handleUpload" :disabled="['uploading', 'success'].includes(status)">
        Upload
      </button>
      <button @click="pauseUpload" :disabled="status !== 'uploading'">
        Pause
      </button>
      <button @click="resumeUpload" :disabled="status !== 'pause'">
        Resume
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="progress-wrapper" v-if="file">
      <p>Status: {{ status }}</p>
      <p>Total Progress: {{ totalPercentage }}%</p>
      <div class="progress-bar">
        <div class="progress" :style="{ width: totalPercentage + '%' }"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script setup>
import { ref, computed } from 'vue';
import axios from 'axios';
import SparkMD5 from 'spark-md5';

// Configuration
const CHUNK_SIZE = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5MB per chunk
const API_BASE = 'http://localhost:3000';

// State
const file = ref(null);
const fileHash = ref('');
const chunkList = ref([]);
const status = ref('wait'); // wait, calculating, uploading, pause, success
const abortControllers = ref([]); // For pausing requests

// Computed total progress
const totalPercentage = computed(() => {
  if (!file.value || !chunkList.value.length) return 0;
  const loaded = chunkList.value.reduce((acc, cur) => acc + cur.chunk.size * cur.percentage, 0);
  return Math.min(100, Math.round(loaded / file.value.size));
});

// 1. Handle file selection
const handleFileChange = (e) => {
  const selectedFile = e.target.files[0];
  if (!selectedFile) return;
  file.value = selectedFile;
  status.value = 'wait';
  chunkList.value = [];
};

// 2. Create file chunks
const createFileChunks = (file, size = CHUNK_SIZE) => {
  const chunks = [];
  let cur = 0;
  while (cur < file.size) {
    chunks.push({ file: file.slice(cur, cur + size) });
    cur += size;
  }
  return chunks;
};

// 3. Calculate file hash (MD5) incrementally to prevent UI blocking
const calculateHash = (chunks) => {
  return new Promise((resolve) => {
    const spark = new SparkMD5.ArrayBuffer();
    let count = 0;
    const reader = new FileReader();

    reader.onload = (e) => {
      spark.append(e.target.result);
      count++;
      if (count === chunks.length) {
        resolve(spark.end());
      } else {
        loadNext();
      }
    };

    const loadNext = () => {
      reader.readAsArrayBuffer(chunks[count].file);
    };
    loadNext();
  });
};

// 4. Verify if file or chunks already exist on server
const verifyUpload = async (filename, hash) => {
  const { data } = await axios.post(`${API_BASE}/verify`, { filename, hash });
  return data;
};

// 5. Upload chunks
const uploadChunks = async (uploadedList = []) => {
  const requests = chunkList.value
    .filter((chunk) => !uploadedList.includes(chunk.hash)) // Filter out already uploaded chunks
    .map((chunk) => {
      const formData = new FormData();
      formData.append('chunk', chunk.chunk);
      formData.append('hash', chunk.hash);
      formData.append('filename', file.value.name);
      formData.append('fileHash', fileHash.value);

      const controller = new AbortController();
      abortControllers.value.push(controller);

      return axios.post(`${API_BASE}/upload`, formData, {
        signal: controller.signal,
        onUploadProgress: (progressEvent) => {
          chunk.percentage = progressEvent.loaded / progressEvent.total;
        },
      }).then(() => {
        // Remove controller when done
        abortControllers.value = abortControllers.value.filter(c => c !== controller);
      });
    });

  await Promise.all(requests);
};

// 6. Merge chunks on server
const mergeRequest = async () => {
  await axios.post(`${API_BASE}/merge`, {
    filename: file.value.name,
    fileHash: fileHash.value,
    size: CHUNK_SIZE,
  });
  status.value = 'success';
};

// Main Upload Flow
const handleUpload = async () => {
  if (!file.value) return;
  status.value = 'calculating';

  // Step 1: Slice
  const chunks = createFileChunks(file.value);

  // Step 2: Hash
  fileHash.value = await calculateHash(chunks);

  // Step 3: Verify
  const { shouldUpload, uploadedList } = await verifyUpload(file.value.name, fileHash.value);

  if (!shouldUpload) {
    status.value = 'success';
    chunkList.value.forEach(chunk => chunk.percentage = 1);
    alert('File already exists (Fast Upload)!');
    return;
  }

  // Initialize chunk list state
  chunkList.value = chunks.map((chunk, index) => ({
    chunk: chunk.file,
    hash: `${fileHash.value}-${index}`,
    index,
    percentage: uploadedList.includes(`${fileHash.value}-${index}`) ? 1 : 0,
  }));

  status.value = 'uploading';

  // Step 4: Upload
  try {
    await uploadChunks(uploadedList);

    // Step 5: Merge
    if (status.value === 'uploading') {
      await mergeRequest();
    }
  } catch (error) {
    if (axios.isCancel(error)) {
      console.log('Upload paused');
    } else {
      console.error('Upload failed', error);
      status.value = 'wait';
    }
  }
};

// Pause Upload
const pauseUpload = () => {
  status.value = 'pause';
  abortControllers.value.forEach(controller => controller.abort());
  abortControllers.value = [];
};

// Resume Upload
const resumeUpload = () => {
  status.value = 'uploading';
  handleUpload(); // Re-run the flow, verify will skip uploaded chunks
};
</script>

<style scoped>
.upload-container { max-width: 500px; margin: 50px auto; font-family: sans-serif; }
.controls { margin: 20px 0; display: flex; gap: 10px; }
button { padding: 8px 16px; cursor: pointer; }
button:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; opacity: 0.5; }
.progress-bar { width: 100%; height: 20px; background: #eee; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; }
.progress { height: 100%; background: #4caf50; transition: width 0.2s ease; }
</style>
```

### 2. Backend: Node.js (Express) Implementation

To make the frontend work, you need a backend to receive, store, and merge the chunks. 

Create a new folder, initialize it (`npm init -y`), and install dependencies:
```bash
npm install express cors express-fileupload fs-extra
```

Create `server.js`:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const cors = require('cors');
const fileUpload = require('express-fileupload');
const fse = require('fs-extra');
const path = require('path');

const app = express();
app.use(cors());
app.use(express.json());
app.use(fileUpload());

const UPLOAD_DIR = path.resolve(__dirname, 'uploads');

// Helper: Extract file extension
const extractExt = filename => filename.slice(filename.lastIndexOf('.'), filename.length);

// 1. Verify if file or chunks exist
app.post('/verify', async (req, res) => {
  const { filename, hash } = req.body;
  const ext = extractExt(filename);
  const filePath = path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, `${hash}${ext}`);
  const chunkDir = path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, hash);

  // If file already exists (Fast upload)
  if (fse.existsSync(filePath)) {
    return res.json({ shouldUpload: false });
  }

  // If chunks exist, return their names for breakpoint continuation
  let uploadedList = [];
  if (fse.existsSync(chunkDir)) {
    uploadedList = await fse.readdir(chunkDir);
  }

  res.json({ shouldUpload: true, uploadedList });
});

// 2. Handle chunk upload
app.post('/upload', async (req, res) => {
  const { hash, fileHash } = req.body;
  const chunk = req.files.chunk;
  const chunkDir = path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, fileHash);

  if (!fse.existsSync(chunkDir)) {
    await fse.mkdirs(chunkDir);
  }

  await chunk.mv(path.resolve(chunkDir, hash));
  res.status(200).send('Chunk uploaded');
});

// 3. Merge chunks
app.post('/merge', async (req, res) => {
  const { filename, fileHash, size } = req.body;
  const ext = extractExt(filename);
  const filePath = path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, `${fileHash}${ext}`);
  const chunkDir = path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, fileHash);

  const chunkPaths = await fse.readdir(chunkDir);

  // Sort chunks by index to ensure correct order
  chunkPaths.sort((a, b) => a.split('-')[1] - b.split('-')[1]);

  const writeStreams = chunkPaths.map((chunkPath, index) => {
    return new Promise((resolve) => {
      const readStream = fse.createReadStream(path.resolve(chunkDir, chunkPath));
      const writeStream = fse.createWriteStream(filePath, {
        start: index * size,
      });
      readStream.on('end', () => {
        fse.unlinkSync(path.resolve(chunkDir, chunkPath)); // Delete chunk after merging
        resolve();
      });
      readStream.pipe(writeStream);
    });
  });

  await Promise.all(writeStreams);
  fse.rmdirSync(chunkDir); // Delete chunk directory

  res.status(200).send('File merged successfully');
});

app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server listening on port 3000');
  if (!fse.existsSync(UPLOAD_DIR)) fse.mkdirsSync(UPLOAD_DIR);
});
```

### How to run the demonstration:

1. Start the Node.js backend: `node server.js` (It will run on port 3000).
2. Run your Vue 3 application (usually `npm run dev`).
3. Select a large file (e.g., a 50MB video).
4. Click **Upload**. You will see the progress bar move.
5. Click **Pause**. The network requests will be aborted.
6. Click **Resume**. The frontend will ask the backend which chunks are already there, skip them, and only upload the remaining chunks.
7. Once it reaches 100%, check the `uploads` folder in your backend directory. You will see the fully merged file.

To display a real-time video stream from a Hikvision camera on a Linux Java Swing application, we must work around the limitation that the Linux Hikvision SDK cannot directly render to a Java window handle (unlike Windows where you can pass an `HWND`).

The standard approach on Linux is:
1. Use `HCNetSDK` to connect to the camera and start a real-time stream with a **RealData Callback**.
2. Pass the stream data received in the callback to the Hikvision **PlayCtrl** decoding library.
3. Set a **Decode Callback** in the PlayCtrl library to receive uncompressed video frames (usually in YV12 / YUV420P format).
4. Convert the YUV data to RGB, construct a `BufferedImage`, and draw it onto a `JPanel`.

Below is a complete, compilable Java Swing demo using JNA. 

### Prerequisites
1. Add **JNA** (`jna.jar`) to your project dependencies.
2. Ensure the Hikvision Linux SDK `.so` files (e.g., `libhcnetsdk.so`, `libPlayCtrl.so`, and their dependencies) are in your system's library path (e.g., `/usr/lib` or specified via `-Djna.library.path=/path/to/sdk`).

### Java Source Code (`HikvisionLinuxDemo.java`)

```java
import com.sun.jna.Library;
import com.sun.jna.Native;
import com.sun.jna.Pointer;
import com.sun.jna.ptr.IntByReference;

import javax.swing.*;
import java.awt.*;
import java.awt.image.BufferedImage;
import java.awt.image.DataBufferInt;

public class HikvisionLinuxDemo extends JFrame {

    private VideoPanel videoPanel;
    private int lUserID = -1;
    private int lPreviewHandle = -1;
    private int port = -1;

    public HikvisionLinuxDemo() {
        setTitle("Hikvision Linux Swing Demo");
        setSize(800, 600);
        setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE);

        videoPanel = new VideoPanel();
        add(videoPanel, BorderLayout.CENTER);

        initHikvision();
    }

    private void initHikvision() {
        boolean initSuc = HCNetSDK.INSTANCE.NET_DVR_Init();
        if (!initSuc) {
            System.err.println("SDK Init Failed!");
            return;
        }

        // Login
        HCNetSDK.NET_DVR_DEVICEINFO_V30 deviceInfo = new HCNetSDK.NET_DVR_DEVICEINFO_V30();
        lUserID = HCNetSDK.INSTANCE.NET_DVR_Login_V30("192.168.1.64", (short) 8000, "admin", "password123", deviceInfo);

        if (lUserID < 0) {
            System.err.println("Login Failed! Error Code: " + HCNetSDK.INSTANCE.NET_DVR_GetLastError());
            return;
        }

        // Start Real Play
        HCNetSDK.NET_DVR_CLIENTINFO clientInfo = new HCNetSDK.NET_DVR_CLIENTINFO();
        clientInfo.lChannel = 1;
        clientInfo.lLinkMode = 0;
        clientInfo.hPlayWnd = null; // MUST be null on Linux for callback mode

        lPreviewHandle = HCNetSDK.INSTANCE.NET_DVR_RealPlay_V30(lUserID, clientInfo, realDataCallBack, null, true);
        if (lPreviewHandle < 0) {
            System.err.println("RealPlay Failed! Error Code: " + HCNetSDK.INSTANCE.NET_DVR_GetLastError());
        }
    }

    // 1. Real Data Callback: Receives stream from camera
    private HCNetSDK.FRealDataCallBack_V30 realDataCallBack = new HCNetSDK.FRealDataCallBack_V30() {
        @Override
        public void invoke(int lRealHandle, int dwDataType, Pointer pBuffer, int dwBufSize, Pointer pUser) {
            switch (dwDataType) {
                case HCNetSDK.NET_DVR_SYSHEAD: // System Header
                    IntByReference portRef = new IntByReference();
                    if (!PlayCtrl.INSTANCE.PlayM4_GetPort(portRef)) break;
                    port = portRef.getValue();

                    if (dwBufSize > 0) {
                        PlayCtrl.INSTANCE.PlayM4_SetStreamOpenMode(port, PlayCtrl.STREAME_REALTIME);
                        if (PlayCtrl.INSTANCE.PlayM4_OpenStream(port, pBuffer, dwBufSize, 1024 * 1024)) {
                            // Set Decode Callback
                            PlayCtrl.INSTANCE.PlayM4_SetDecCallBack(port, decodeCallback);
                            PlayCtrl.INSTANCE.PlayM4_Play(port, null);
                        }
                    }
                    break;
                case HCNetSDK.NET_DVR_STREAMDATA: // Video Stream Data
                    if (dwBufSize > 0 && port != -1) {
                        PlayCtrl.INSTANCE.PlayM4_InputData(port, pBuffer, dwBufSize);
                    }
                    break;
            }
        }
    };

    // 2. Decode Callback: Receives YUV frames from PlayCtrl
    private PlayCtrl.DecCBFun decodeCallback = new PlayCtrl.DecCBFun() {
        @Override
        public void invoke(int nPort, Pointer pBuf, int nSize, PlayCtrl.FRAME_INFO pFrameInfo, int nReserved1, int nReserved2) {
            if (pFrameInfo.nType == 3) { // Video frame (YV12)
                int width = pFrameInfo.nWidth;
                int height = pFrameInfo.nHeight;

                // Convert YV12 to RGB and update the panel
                byte[] yv12Data = pBuf.getByteArray(0, nSize);
                BufferedImage image = YV12ToBufferedImage(yv12Data, width, height);

                SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() -> videoPanel.setImage(image));
            }
        }
    };

    // Basic YV12 to RGB conversion (For production, consider OpenCV or hardware acceleration for performance)
    private BufferedImage YV12ToBufferedImage(byte[] yv12, int width, int height) {
        BufferedImage image = new BufferedImage(width, height, BufferedImage.TYPE_INT_RGB);
        int[] rgbData = ((DataBufferInt) image.getRaster().getDataBuffer()).getData();

        int frameSize = width * height;
        int yIndex = 0;
        int vIndex = frameSize;
        int uIndex = frameSize + (frameSize / 4);

        int r, g, b, y, u, v;
        for (int j = 0; j < height; j++) {
            for (int i = 0; i < width; i++) {
                y = (0xff & yv12[yIndex]) - 16;
                if (y < 0) y = 0;

                v = (0xff & yv12[vIndex]) - 128;
                u = (0xff & yv12[uIndex]) - 128;

                int y1192 = 1192 * y;
                r = (y1192 + 1634 * v);
                g = (y1192 - 833 * v - 400 * u);
                b = (y1192 + 2066 * u);

                r = Math.max(0, Math.min(262143, r));
                g = Math.max(0, Math.min(262143, g));
                b = Math.max(0, Math.min(262143, b));

                rgbData[yIndex++] = ((r << 6) & 0xff0000) | ((g >> 2) & 0xff00) | ((b >> 10) & 0xff);

                if ((i & 1) == 1) {
                    uIndex++;
                    vIndex++;
                }
            }
            if ((j & 1) == 0) {
                uIndex -= (width >> 1);
                vIndex -= (width >> 1);
            }
        }
        return image;
    }

    // Custom JPanel to draw the BufferedImage
    class VideoPanel extends JPanel {
        private BufferedImage currentImage;

        public void setImage(BufferedImage image) {
            this.currentImage = image;
            repaint();
        }

        @Override
        protected void paintComponent(Graphics g) {
            super.paintComponent(g);
            if (currentImage != null) {
                g.drawImage(currentImage, 0, 0, getWidth(), getHeight(), this);
            } else {
                g.setColor(Color.BLACK);
                g.fillRect(0, 0, getWidth(), getHeight());
                g.setColor(Color.WHITE);
                g.drawString("Waiting for video stream...", 20, 20);
            }
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() -> {
            new HikvisionLinuxDemo().setVisible(true);
        });
    }

    // --- JNA MAPPINGS ---

    public interface HCNetSDK extends Library {
        HCNetSDK INSTANCE = Native.load("hcnetsdk", HCNetSDK.class);

        int NET_DVR_SYSHEAD = 1;
        int NET_DVR_STREAMDATA = 2;

        boolean NET_DVR_Init();
        int NET_DVR_Login_V30(String sDVRIP, short wDVRPort, String sUserName, String sPassword, NET_DVR_DEVICEINFO_V30 lpDeviceInfo);
        int NET_DVR_RealPlay_V30(int lUserID, NET_DVR_CLIENTINFO lpClientInfo, FRealDataCallBack_V30 fRealDataCallBack_V30, Pointer pUser, boolean bBlocked);
        int NET_DVR_GetLastError();

        class NET_DVR_DEVICEINFO_V30 extends com.sun.jna.Structure {
            public byte[] sSerialNumber = new byte[48];
            public byte byAlarmInPortNum;
            public byte byAlarmOutPortNum;
            public byte byDiskNum;
            public byte byDVRType;
            public byte byChanNum;
            public byte byStartChan;
            public byte byAudioChanNum;
            public byte byIPChanNum;
            public byte[] byRes1 = new byte[24];
            @Override protected java.util.List<String> getFieldOrder() {
                return java.util.Arrays.asList("sSerialNumber", "byAlarmInPortNum", "byAlarmOutPortNum", "byDiskNum", "byDVRType", "byChanNum", "byStartChan", "byAudioChanNum", "byIPChanNum", "byRes1");
            }
        }

        class NET_DVR_CLIENTINFO extends com.sun.jna.Structure {
            public int lChannel;
            public int lLinkMode;
            public Pointer hPlayWnd;
            public String sMultiCastIP;
            @Override protected java.util.List<String> getFieldOrder() {
                return java.util.Arrays.asList("lChannel", "lLinkMode", "hPlayWnd", "sMultiCastIP");
            }
        }

        interface FRealDataCallBack_V30 extends com.sun.jna.Callback {
            void invoke(int lRealHandle, int dwDataType, Pointer pBuffer, int dwBufSize, Pointer pUser);
        }
    }

    public interface PlayCtrl extends Library {
        PlayCtrl INSTANCE = Native.load("PlayCtrl", PlayCtrl.class);

        int STREAME_REALTIME = 0;

        boolean PlayM4_GetPort(IntByReference nPort);
        boolean PlayM4_SetStreamOpenMode(int nPort, int nMode);
        boolean PlayM4_OpenStream(int nPort, Pointer pFileHeadBuf, int nSize, int nBufPoolSize);
        boolean PlayM4_Play(int nPort, Pointer hWnd);
        boolean PlayM4_InputData(int nPort, Pointer pBuf, int nSize);
        boolean PlayM4_SetDecCallBack(int nPort, DecCBFun DecCBFun);

        class FRAME_INFO extends com.sun.jna.Structure {
            public int nWidth;
            public int nHeight;
            public int nStamp;
            public int nType;
            public int nFrameRate;
            public int dwFrameNum;
            @Override protected java.util.List<String> getFieldOrder() {
                return java.util.Arrays.asList("nWidth", "nHeight", "nStamp", "nType", "nFrameRate", "dwFrameNum");
            }
        }

        interface DecCBFun extends com.sun.jna.Callback {
            void invoke(int nPort, Pointer pBuf, int nSize, FRAME_INFO pFrameInfo, int nReserved1, int nReserved2);
        }
    }
}
```

### Key Technical Details:
1. **`hPlayWnd = null`**: In `NET_DVR_CLIENTINFO`, the window handle is explicitly set to `null`. This tells the SDK not to attempt hardware rendering.
2. **Stream Pipeline**: `Camera -> HCNetSDK (RealDataCallBack) -> PlayCtrl (InputData) -> PlayCtrl (DecCBFun) -> YV12 Byte Array -> Java BufferedImage -> JPanel`.
3. **YV12 to RGB Conversion**: The `YV12ToBufferedImage` method performs a software-based color space conversion. *Note: Software conversion in pure Java can be CPU intensive for 1080p+ streams. For production environments, it is highly recommended to use JNI with libyuv, OpenCV, or OpenGL shaders to handle the YUV-to-RGB conversion.*
4. **Thread Safety**: The `DecCBFun` callback is invoked by a native Hikvision thread. We must use `SwingUtilities.invokeLater()` to safely pass the generated `BufferedImage` to the Swing Event Dispatch Thread (EDT) for rendering.

Here is a complete, executable HTML5 2D top-down game prototype that includes all the requested features. It uses vanilla JavaScript and HTML5 Canvas, requiring no external libraries. 

You can save the code below as an `.html` file (e.g., `game.html`) and open it in any modern web browser (desktop or mobile).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no">
    <title>HTML5 Open World Prototype</title>
    <style>
        body, html { margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background-color: #333; font-family: sans-serif; user-select: none; }
        canvas { display: block; }
        #ui-layer { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; }
        #mission-panel { position: absolute; top: 10px; left: 10px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.7); color: white; padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px; pointer-events: auto; }

        /* Virtual Controls */
        #joystick-zone { position: absolute; bottom: 20px; left: 20px; width: 120px; height: 120px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2); border-radius: 50%; pointer-events: auto; touch-action: none; }
        #joystick-knob { position: absolute; top: 35px; left: 35px; width: 50px; height: 50px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); border-radius: 50%; pointer-events: none; }

        .action-btn { position: absolute; bottom: 20px; width: 70px; height: 70px; background: rgba(255,0,0,0.5); color: white; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid white; font-weight: bold; pointer-events: auto; touch-action: none; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; text-align: center; font-size: 12px; }
        #btn-attack { right: 100px; background: rgba(255, 100, 0, 0.6); }
        #btn-interact { right: 20px; background: rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.6); }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<canvas id="gameCanvas"></canvas>

<div id="ui-layer">
    <div id="mission-panel">
        <strong>Mission:</strong> <span id="mission-text">Loading...</span>
    </div>

    <div id="joystick-zone">
        <div id="joystick-knob"></div>
    </div>

    <div id="btn-attack" class="action-btn">SHOOT</div>
    <div id="btn-interact" class="action-btn">ENTER<br>VEHICLE</div>
</div>

<script>
const canvas = document.getElementById('gameCanvas');
const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

// Resize canvas
function resize() {
    canvas.width = window.innerWidth;
    canvas.height = window.innerHeight;
}
window.addEventListener('resize', resize);
resize();

// Game Constants
const MAP_SIZE = 3000;
const TILE_SIZE = 100;

// Input State
const input = { x: 0, y: 0, interact: false, attack: false };

// Joystick Logic
const joyZone = document.getElementById('joystick-zone');
const joyKnob = document.getElementById('joystick-knob');
let joyActive = false;
let joyCenter = { x: 0, y: 0 };

function handleJoyStart(e) {
    joyActive = true;
    const rect = joyZone.getBoundingClientRect();
    joyCenter = { x: rect.left + rect.width / 2, y: rect.top + rect.height / 2 };
    handleJoyMove(e);
}
function handleJoyMove(e) {
    if (!joyActive) return;
    e.preventDefault();
    const touch = e.touches ? e.touches[0] : e;
    let dx = touch.clientX - joyCenter.x;
    let dy = touch.clientY - joyCenter.y;
    const distance = Math.min(Math.hypot(dx, dy), 35);
    const angle = Math.atan2(dy, dx);

    const knobX = Math.cos(angle) * distance;
    const knobY = Math.sin(angle) * distance;
    joyKnob.style.transform = `translate(${knobX}px, ${knobY}px)`;

    input.x = Math.cos(angle) * (distance / 35);
    input.y = Math.sin(angle) * (distance / 35);
}
function handleJoyEnd() {
    joyActive = false;
    joyKnob.style.transform = `translate(0px, 0px)`;
    input.x = 0;
    input.y = 0;
}

joyZone.addEventListener('mousedown', handleJoyStart);
window.addEventListener('mousemove', handleJoyMove);
window.addEventListener('mouseup', handleJoyEnd);
joyZone.addEventListener('touchstart', handleJoyStart, {passive: false});
window.addEventListener('touchmove', handleJoyMove, {passive: false});
window.addEventListener('touchend', handleJoyEnd);

// Action Buttons
document.getElementById('btn-interact').addEventListener('mousedown', () => input.interact = true);
document.getElementById('btn-interact').addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); input.interact = true; });
document.getElementById('btn-attack').addEventListener('mousedown', () => input.attack = true);
document.getElementById('btn-attack').addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); input.attack = true; });

// Keyboard fallback
window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if(e.key === 'w') input.y = -1;
    if(e.key === 's') input.y = 1;
    if(e.key === 'a') input.x = -1;
    if(e.key === 'd') input.x = 1;
    if(e.key === 'e') input.interact = true;
    if(e.key === ' ') input.attack = true;
});
window.addEventListener('keyup', (e) => {
    if(e.key === 'w' || e.key === 's') input.y = 0;
    if(e.key === 'a' || e.key === 'd') input.x = 0;
});

// Game Classes
class Entity {
    constructor(x, y, radius, color) {
        this.x = x; this.y = y;
        this.radius = radius; this.color = color;
        this.vx = 0; this.vy = 0;
        this.speed = 3;
        this.hp = 100;
        this.dead = false;
        this.angle = 0;
    }
    update() {
        this.x += this.vx;
        this.y += this.vy;
        // Map bounds
        this.x = Math.max(this.radius, Math.min(MAP_SIZE - this.radius, this.x));
        this.y = Math.max(this.radius, Math.min(MAP_SIZE - this.radius, this.y));
    }
    draw(ctx) {
        ctx.save();
        ctx.translate(this.x, this.y);
        ctx.rotate(this.angle);
        ctx.fillStyle = this.color;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(0, 0, this.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
        // Direction indicator
        ctx.fillStyle = 'black';
        ctx.fillRect(0, -2, this.radius + 5, 4);
        ctx.restore();
    }
}

class Vehicle {
    constructor(x, y) {
        this.x = x; this.y = y;
        this.width = 80; this.height = 40;
        this.angle = 0;
        this.driver = null; // null, 'player', or NPC object
        this.speed = 0;
        this.maxSpeed = 12;
    }
    update() {
        if (this.driver) {
            this.x += Math.cos(this.angle) * this.speed;
            this.y += Math.sin(this.angle) * this.speed;
            this.speed *= 0.95; // friction
        }
        this.x = Math.max(this.width, Math.min(MAP_SIZE - this.width, this.x));
        this.y = Math.max(this.height, Math.min(MAP_SIZE - this.height, this.y));
    }
    draw(ctx) {
        ctx.save();
        ctx.translate(this.x, this.y);
        ctx.rotate(this.angle);
        ctx.fillStyle = this.driver === 'player' ? '#00ff00' : (this.driver ? '#ff5555' : '#aaaaaa');
        ctx.fillRect(-this.width/2, -this.height/2, this.width, this.height);
        // Windshield
        ctx.fillStyle = '#88ccff';
        ctx.fillRect(10, -this.height/2 + 5, 15, this.height - 10);
        ctx.restore();
    }
}

class Bullet {
    constructor(x, y, angle, isPlayer) {
        this.x = x; this.y = y;
        this.vx = Math.cos(angle) * 15;
        this.vy = Math.sin(angle) * 15;
        this.life = 60;
        this.isPlayer = isPlayer;
    }
    update() {
        this.x += this.vx;
        this.y += this.vy;
        this.life--;
    }
    draw(ctx) {
        ctx.fillStyle = 'yellow';
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(this.x, this.y, 4, 0, Math.PI*2);
        ctx.fill();
    }
}

// Game State
const player = new Entity(MAP_SIZE/2, MAP_SIZE/2, 15, '#0088ff');
let playerInVehicle = null;
let lastShootTime = 0;

const vehicles = [];
const npcs = [];
const bullets = [];

// Populate Map
for(let i=0; i<10; i++) {
    let v = new Vehicle(Math.random() * MAP_SIZE, Math.random() * MAP_SIZE);
    // 50% chance NPC is driving
    if (Math.random() > 0.5) {
        let npc = new Entity(v.x, v.y, 15, '#ff0000');
        v.driver = npc;
        npcs.push(npc);
    }
    vehicles.push(v);
}
for(let i=0; i<15; i++) {
    npcs.push(new Entity(Math.random() * MAP_SIZE, Math.random() * MAP_SIZE, 15, '#ff0000'));
}

// Mission System
const missions = [
    { text: "Steal a vehicle from an NPC", check: () => playerInVehicle && npcs.some(n => n.justKickedOut) },
    { text: "Defeat 3 NPCs", target: 3, count: 0, check: function() { return this.count >= this.target; } },
    { text: "Drive to the edge of the map", check: () => player.x < 100 || player.x > MAP_SIZE-100 || player.y < 100 || player.y > MAP_SIZE-100 }
];
let currentMission = 0;

function updateMission() {
    const mText = document.getElementById('mission-text');
    if (currentMission < missions.length) {
        mText.innerText = missions[currentMission].text + (missions[currentMission].target ? ` (${missions[currentMission].count}/${missions[currentMission].target})` : '');
        if (missions[currentMission].check()) {
            currentMission++;
            if(currentMission >= missions.length) mText.innerText = "All missions completed!";
        }
    }
}

// Main Loop
function update() {
    // Player Movement & Logic
    if (!playerInVehicle) {
        player.vx = input.x * player.speed;
        player.vy = input.y * player.speed;
        if (input.x !== 0 || input.y !== 0) player.angle = Math.atan2(input.y, input.x);
        player.update();

        // Shooting
        if (input.attack && Date.now() - lastShootTime > 300) {
            bullets.push(new Bullet(player.x, player.y, player.angle, true));
            lastShootTime = Date.now();
        }
    } else {
        // Driving
        if (input.y < 0) playerInVehicle.speed += 0.5; // Forward
        if (input.y > 0) playerInVehicle.speed -= 0.5; // Reverse/Brake
        if (input.x !== 0) playerInVehicle.angle += input.x * 0.05; // Steer

        playerInVehicle.speed = Math.max(-playerInVehicle.maxSpeed/2, Math.min(playerInVehicle.maxSpeed, playerInVehicle.speed));
        player.x = playerInVehicle.x;
        player.y = playerInVehicle.y;
    }

    // Interaction (Enter/Exit/Steal Vehicle)
    if (input.interact) {
        input.interact = false; // consume input
        if (playerInVehicle) {
            // Exit
            player.x -= Math.cos(playerInVehicle.angle) * 50;
            player.y -= Math.sin(playerInVehicle.angle) * 50;
            playerInVehicle.driver = null;
            playerInVehicle = null;
            document.getElementById('btn-interact').innerHTML = "ENTER<br>VEHICLE";
        } else {
            // Find nearest vehicle
            let nearest = null;
            let minDist = 100;
            vehicles.forEach(v => {
                let dist = Math.hypot(v.x - player.x, v.y - player.y);
                if (dist < minDist) { minDist = dist; nearest = v; }
            });

            if (nearest) {
                if (nearest.driver && nearest.driver !== 'player') {
                    // Steal! Kick NPC out
                    let npc = nearest.driver;
                    npc.x = nearest.x - Math.cos(nearest.angle) * 50;
                    npc.y = nearest.y - Math.sin(nearest.angle) * 50;
                    npc.justKickedOut = true; // For mission
                }
                nearest.driver = 'player';
                playerInVehicle = nearest;
                document.getElementById('btn-interact').innerHTML = "EXIT<br>VEHICLE";
            }
        }
    }

    // Update Vehicles
    vehicles.forEach(v => v.update());

    // Update NPCs
    npcs.forEach(npc => {
        if (npc.dead) return;

        // Simple AI: Wander or chase if close
        let distToPlayer = Math.hypot(player.x - npc.x, player.y - npc.y);

        // Check if NPC is driving
        let drivingVehicle = vehicles.find(v => v.driver === npc);

        if (drivingVehicle) {
            drivingVehicle.speed = 4;
            drivingVehicle.angle += (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.1;
            npc.x = drivingVehicle.x;
            npc.y = drivingVehicle.y;
        } else {
            if (distToPlayer < 300 && !playerInVehicle) {
                // Chase
                npc.angle = Math.atan2(player.y - npc.y, player.x - npc.x);
                npc.vx = Math.cos(npc.angle) * (npc.speed * 0.8);
                npc.vy = Math.sin(npc.angle) * (npc.speed * 0.8);
            } else {
                // Wander
                if (Math.random() < 0.02) npc.angle += (Math.random() - 0.5) * Math.PI;
                npc.vx = Math.cos(npc.angle) * (npc.speed * 0.3);
                npc.vy = Math.sin(npc.angle) * (npc.speed * 0.3);
            }
            npc.update();
        }
    });

    // Update Bullets & Collision
    for (let i = bullets.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        let b = bullets[i];
        b.update();
        if (b.life <= 0) { bullets.splice(i, 1); continue; }

        if (b.isPlayer) {
            npcs.forEach(npc => {
                if (!npc.dead && Math.hypot(npc.x - b.x, npc.y - b.y) < npc.radius + 5) {
                    npc.hp -= 50;
                    bullets.splice(i, 1);
                    if (npc.hp <= 0) {
                        npc.dead = true;
                        if(currentMission < missions.length && missions[currentMission].target) {
                            missions[currentMission].count++;
                        }
                    }
                }
            });
        }
    }

    updateMission();
}

function draw() {
    // Camera follows player
    const camX = player.x - canvas.width / 2;
    const camY = player.y - canvas.height / 2;

    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
    ctx.save();
    ctx.translate(-camX, -camY);

    // Draw Map Grid (Grass/Street feel)
    ctx.fillStyle = '#4CAF50';
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, MAP_SIZE, MAP_SIZE);
    ctx.strokeStyle = '#388E3C';
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    for(let x=0; x<=MAP_SIZE; x+=TILE_SIZE) {
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x, 0); ctx.lineTo(x, MAP_SIZE); ctx.stroke();
    }
    for(let y=0; y<=MAP_SIZE; y+=TILE_SIZE) {
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(0, y); ctx.lineTo(MAP_SIZE, y); ctx.stroke();
    }

    // Draw Entities
    vehicles.forEach(v => v.draw(ctx));
    npcs.forEach(npc => { if(!npc.dead && !vehicles.find(v=>v.driver===npc)) npc.draw(ctx); });

    if (!playerInVehicle) player.draw(ctx);

    bullets.forEach(b => b.draw(ctx));

    ctx.restore();
}

function loop() {
    update();
    draw();
    requestAnimationFrame(loop);
}

// Start Game
loop();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Here is a complete, executable single-file web game using HTML, CSS, and the **Three.js** library for 3D rendering. 

This game features a spacecraft that you can pilot through a 3D star system. The planets exert a gravitational pull on your ship based on Newton's law of universal gravitation ($F = G \frac{m_1 m_2}{r^2}$). You must use your thrusters to navigate, orbit, or escape the gravitational wells of the planets.

### How to play:
Save the code below as an `.html` file (e.g., `space_game.html`) and open it in any modern web browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>3D Gravity Spacecraft Game</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            overflow: hidden;
            background-color: #000;
            color: white;
            font-family: sans-serif;
        }
        #ui {
            position: absolute;
            top: 10px;
            left: 10px;
            background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: 1px solid #444;
            pointer-events: none;
        }
        h1 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 20px; color: #00ffcc; }
        p { margin: 5px 0; font-size: 14px; }
        .key { background: #333; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; }
    </style>
    <!-- Load Three.js -->
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>

    <div id="ui">
        <h1>Orbital Escape</h1>
        <p><span class="key">W</span> / <span class="key">S</span> : Thrust Forward / Backward</p>
        <p><span class="key">A</span> / <span class="key">D</span> : Turn Left / Right (Yaw)</p>
        <p><span class="key">↑</span> / <span class="key">↓</span> : Pitch Up / Down</p>
        <p id="speedDisplay">Speed: 0.00</p>
    </div>

    <script>
        // --- Scene Setup ---
        const scene = new THREE.Scene();
        const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(60, window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, 0.1, 10000);
        const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });
        renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
        document.body.appendChild(renderer.domElement);

        // --- Lighting ---
        const ambientLight = new THREE.AmbientLight(0x333333);
        scene.add(ambientLight);
        const sunLight = new THREE.PointLight(0xffffff, 1.5, 5000);
        sunLight.position.set(0, 0, 0);
        scene.add(sunLight);

        // --- Starfield Background ---
        const starsGeometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        const starsMaterial = new THREE.PointsMaterial({color: 0xffffff, size: 0.5});
        const starsVertices = [];
        for(let i=0; i<5000; i++) {
            const x = THREE.MathUtils.randFloatSpread(2000);
            const y = THREE.MathUtils.randFloatSpread(2000);
            const z = THREE.MathUtils.randFloatSpread(2000);
            starsVertices.push(x, y, z);
        }
        starsGeometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(starsVertices, 3));
        const starField = new THREE.Points(starsGeometry, starsMaterial);
        scene.add(starField);

        // --- Spacecraft ---
        const shipGeometry = new THREE.ConeGeometry(0.5, 2, 16);
        shipGeometry.rotateX(Math.PI / 2); // Point the cone along the Z axis
        const shipMaterial = new THREE.MeshPhongMaterial({ color: 0x00ffcc, flatShading: true });
        const ship = new THREE.Mesh(shipGeometry, shipMaterial);
        ship.position.set(0, 0, 100);
        scene.add(ship);

        // --- Planets & Physics Setup ---
        const G = 0.5; // Gravitational constant (scaled for gameplay)
        const planets = [];

        function createPlanet(radius, mass, color, x, y, z, isSun = false) {
            const geo = new THREE.SphereGeometry(radius, 32, 32);
            const mat = isSun 
                ? new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: color }) 
                : new THREE.MeshPhongMaterial({ color: color });
            const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);
            mesh.position.set(x, y, z);
            scene.add(mesh);
            planets.push({ mesh, mass, radius });
        }

        // Create a central "Sun" and some planets
        createPlanet(15, 500, 0xffdd00, 0, 0, 0, true); // Sun
        createPlanet(5, 100, 0x0044ff, 150, 0, 0);      // Blue Planet
        createPlanet(8, 200, 0xff4400, -200, 50, -100); // Red Planet
        createPlanet(3, 50, 0xaaaaaa, 0, -100, 150);    // Gray Moon

        // Ship Physics State
        const velocity = new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, 0);
        const thrustPower = 0.02;
        const turnSpeed = 0.03;

        // --- Controls ---
        const keys = {};
        window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => keys[e.code] = true);
        window.addEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys[e.code] = false);

        // --- Game Loop ---
        const speedDisplay = document.getElementById('speedDisplay');

        function animate() {
            requestAnimationFrame(animate);

            // 1. Handle Input (Rotation & Thrust)
            if (keys['KeyA']) ship.rotateY(turnSpeed);
            if (keys['KeyD']) ship.rotateY(-turnSpeed);
            if (keys['ArrowUp']) ship.rotateX(-turnSpeed);
            if (keys['ArrowDown']) ship.rotateX(turnSpeed);

            // Calculate forward direction based on ship's current rotation
            const forward = new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, 1).applyQuaternion(ship.quaternion);

            if (keys['KeyW']) {
                velocity.add(forward.clone().multiplyScalar(thrustPower));
            }
            if (keys['KeyS']) {
                velocity.add(forward.clone().multiplyScalar(-thrustPower));
            }

            // 2. Apply Gravity from all planets
            planets.forEach(planet => {
                const direction = new THREE.Vector3().subVectors(planet.mesh.position, ship.position);
                const distanceSq = direction.lengthSq();
                const distance = Math.sqrt(distanceSq);

                // Only apply gravity if outside the planet (prevent infinite gravity at center)
                if (distance > planet.radius) {
                    // F = G * (m1 * m2) / r^2. Ship mass is assumed to be 1.
                    const forceMagnitude = (G * planet.mass) / distanceSq;
                    direction.normalize().multiplyScalar(forceMagnitude);
                    velocity.add(direction);
                } else {
                    // Collision with planet - bounce back slightly and lose speed
                    velocity.multiplyScalar(-0.5);
                    ship.position.add(direction.normalize().multiplyScalar(-1));
                }
            });

            // 3. Update Ship Position
            ship.position.add(velocity);

            // 4. Update Camera (Follow Ship)
            // Place camera slightly behind and above the ship
            const relativeCameraOffset = new THREE.Vector3(0, 3, -10);
            const cameraOffset = relativeCameraOffset.applyMatrix4(ship.matrixWorld);
            camera.position.lerp(cameraOffset, 0.1);
            camera.lookAt(ship.position);

            // Update UI
            speedDisplay.innerText = `Speed: ${(velocity.length() * 100).toFixed(1)}`;

            // Render
            renderer.render(scene, camera);
        }

        // Handle Window Resize
        window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
            camera.aspect = window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight;
            camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
            renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
        });

        // Start Game
        animate();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Features included:
1. **Real Physics**: The game calculates the distance vector between the ship and every celestial body on every frame. It applies the inverse-square law to calculate gravitational acceleration and modifies the ship's velocity vector accordingly.
2. **Orbital Mechanics**: If you approach a planet at the right speed and angle, you will get caught in its orbit. If you are falling in too fast, you must point your ship away and hold `W` to burn your thrusters and achieve escape velocity.
3. **Full 3D Movement**: You can pitch and yaw your spacecraft to orient yourself in the 3D vacuum of space.
4. **Dynamic Camera**: A chase camera smoothly follows behind your spacecraft, rotating as you rotate.

Here is a complete, executable frontend program using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It simulates the celestial movement of the sun across the sky, complete with a day-to-night color transition and a slider so you can manually control the time of day.

You can save the code below as an `.html` file (e.g., `sun_simulation.html`) and open it in any modern web browser to see it in action.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
