<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Music Theory Hub</h1>
        <p>Learn the fundamentals of Scales and Chords</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <a onclick="showSection('scales')">Scales</a>
        <a onclick="showSection('chords')">Chords</a>
        <a onclick="showSection('practice')">Practice</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- SCALES SECTION -->
        <div id="scales" class="section active">
            <h2>Musical Scales</h2>
            <p>A scale is any set of musical notes ordered by fundamental frequency or pitch. A scale ordered by increasing pitch is an ascending scale, and a scale ordered by decreasing pitch is a descending scale.</p>

            <h3>The Major Scale</h3>
            <p>The major scale is one of the most commonly used musical scales, especially in Western music. It is made up of seven notes. The pattern of whole and half steps is: <strong>Whole, Whole, Half, Whole, Whole, Whole, Half</strong>.</p>
            <button onclick="playScale(['C4', 'D4', 'E4', 'F4', 'G4', 'A4', 'B4', 'C5'])">Listen to C Major Scale</button>

