Creating a fully-fledged 3D WebGL game with real-time volumetric terrain destruction and particle-based fluid simulation requires a massive game engine (like Unity, Unreal, or a complex Three.js/WebGL architecture) and cannot fit into a single script. 

However, we can build a **highly advanced 2D pixel-physics engine** (similar to games like *Noita* or *Worms*) using HTML5, JavaScript, and Canvas pixel manipulation. This approach perfectly demonstrates all your requested mechanics: Perlin noise terrain generation, real-time terrain destruction, cellular automata fluid simulation, and entity movement penalties.

