To build an online webpage screenshot tool, we need to overcome a fundamental web security restriction: browsers do not allow JavaScript to directly capture the screen or render external websites due to Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) and security policies. 

To solve this, we use a **third-party Screenshot API** (in this case, the free `thum.io` API) to render the webpage on a server and return the image to our frontend.

Below is a complete, executable single-file solution containing HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. You can save this code as an `.html` file (e.g., `screenshot.html`) and open it directly in your browser.

### Complete Code (`screenshot.html`)

